Package: graphgenerator
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Moisés Maia Neto <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, libgl1, libegl1, libfontconfig1, libdbus-1-3, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcb-cursor0, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-image0, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xinerama0, libxcb-xkb1
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian
Description: Generate charts (1D/2D/3D) from CSV/XLSX data
 GraphGenerator turns a CSV or XLSX table into a chart: bar, line, scatter,
 stacked/overlapped area, box, violin, histogram, density, heatmap and
 numeric 2D/3D scatter, with trendlines, legends, color palettes and
 export to PNG/JPG/TIFF/PDF/EPS/SVG at a chosen DPI.
 .
 The program is written in Python + PySide6 (Qt). This package installs the
 application in /usr/share/graphgenerator, creates the Menu and Desktop
 shortcut and, at install time, builds a private Python virtual environment
 (/usr/lib/graphgenerator/venv) with PySide6, numpy, pandas, matplotlib,
 seaborn and openpyxl downloaded from PyPI, so it needs internet access
 once and never touches the system Python packages.
